teractive-session item. The c66 stall census proved the grace requests' histories carry +5..+9 anomalous messages (duplicated tool results, assistant-msg runs) -- but the REQUESTS.log START tail cap (2 msgs, iar--reqlog-payload-tail in iar-request-log.el) cannot show WHAT they are. Discriminator: raise the tail cap to 6 msgs to match the roles field (3-line change, same file). No urgency -- the census pattern re-fires on the next stall either way; with the 6-msg tail the next stall would hand us the full mechanism instead of another hypothesis list.</p>\naria-cycle [1788864936]: <p>[aria c68] DRAIN msg 577: the tail-cap flag is RESOLVED -- interactive session landed iar-request-log-tail-msgs=6 (<a href=\"http://i.ar\">i.ar</a> 01533ea, suite 1125/1125). Also found this cycle: the sophon <a href=\"http://i.ar\">i.ar</a> checkout was at 706f4e4 (continuo c133) when c67 started, so c67 ran WITHOUT the budget trailer/600s timeout/6-msg tail -- the ExecStartPre heal fixes ownership, not staleness. Checkout now pulled to 01533ea; next cycles run the new code. No action needed from you beyond the still-open RAGE_KNOWN_HOSTS unit env.</p>\naria-cycle [1788865914]: <p>[aria c69] Flag: gpu-load-probe (continuo's early-morning failure-window instrument) is BUILT but NOT INSTALLED on sophon -- timer inactive, /var/log/gpu-load empty. It fires 00:30 local, probes ~3.5h covering the 00:32-03:55 failure window. Today's census found 3 exit-1 + 5 wall-grazes in that window; the probe's GPU data would discriminate H1 (workload) vs H2 (model degradation). Install = copy knowledge/aria/bin/gpu-load-probe.{service,timer} to /etc/systemd/system + daemon-reload + enable --timer. Host-side, so yours. Not urgent (tonight's window runs instrumented anyway), but it would make tomorrow's census quantitative.</p>\naria-cycle [1788887487]: <p>[aria c84] notes.git mirror missing on rammstein: sophon bare /home/git/repos/notes.git has main=f424f8dcc910 but rammstein /home/git/repos/notes.git does 